  "finalText": "Notes are animated; checking the frames now.\nI built the 12-second scene as a single composition with all three beats overlapping. I checked it only on a contact sheet of still frames. I didn't run the critique tool or play it back. The critic's one note was too many accent colors; I left that because the multi-color notes are what make it read as friendly flat illustration.\n\n- **Beat 1, 0–4s:** six sticky notes (**n1–n6**) pop in with a Back Out stagger. Each has a password written on it, such as \"hunter2\" and \"Pa$$w0rd!\". They jitter with a rotation wobble until about 3.8s. A faint **shield** waits at the right.\n- **Beat 2, 3.6–5.1s:** each note pulls back slightly, then accelerates into the shield on an Expo In curve while shrinking and fading. The shield sharpens to full opacity and bumps with each arrival (spring settle). Beat 1 hands over smoothly because the notes pull back before the shield takes them in.\n- **Beat 3, 7.3–12s:**\n  - A blue **wash** expands from the shield and replaces the cream background.\n  - The shield slides to center and a warm **glow** pulses behind it.\n  - A green **check** draws on.\n  - The **headline** \"One key. Every login.\" slides up with Expo Out.\n\nThe contact sheet showed the check mark visible too early and the wash not covering the full frame. I hid the check until its draw-on and enlarged the wash. In the last check only the 5.47s, 8s, 9s and 12s frames were re-rendered.\n\nThe jitter only moves the notes' rotation, not their position. Say if you want a stronger anxious shake, a calmer end with a subtle shield pulse, or the notes' pile enlarged."
